// ParkParticipant
// Source: /Docs/API-endpoints/13-social-endpoints.md §6
//
// Who is currently in a park. The authoritative answer to "is this park full?"
// and "may this socket speak here?".
//
// This row is *membership*, not presence. It says a user has been admitted; it
// does not say where their creature is standing, which is the gateway's memory.
//
// Why membership is in Postgres and not only in the gateway
// ---------------------------------------------------------
// Because capacity has to be enforced against a lock, and a lock has to be
// somewhere both racing requests can see. Two people taking the last slot at
// the same moment is the canonical bug this feature has, and the fix is a
// `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` on the parent `Park` row inside the transaction that
// inserts here (parks.service.ts). An in-memory counter in one process cannot
// promise that, and across two processes it cannot even be asked.

model ParkParticipant {
  id     String @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  parkId String @db.Uuid
  userId String @db.Uuid

  joinedAt DateTime @default(now())

  /// The heartbeat.
  ///
  /// **This column is the whole disconnect story.** A "leave" event from a
  /// client is a courtesy; a closed laptop, a dead wifi connection and a killed
  /// tab all send nothing at all. So a live participant's socket touches this
  /// column periodically, and the sweeper deletes rows that have stopped being
  /// touched — which is the one definition of "gone" that does not depend on
  /// the client agreeing to say goodbye.
  lastSeenAt DateTime @default(now())

  park Park @relation(fields: [parkId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  user User @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  /// One membership per person per park. A refresh re-joins rather than
  /// occupying a second slot, which is also what stops one user filling a park
  /// on their own by opening tabs.
  @@unique([parkId, userId])
  @@index([parkId])
  @@index([userId])

  /// The sweeper's index: everything that has stopped breathing.
  @@index([lastSeenAt])
}
